// tests/fixtures/err_unique_missing_type_argument.ubl
// Unique<T>/Shared<T>/SyncShared<T> take exactly one type argument, the
// same arity check every other single-argument generic wrapper gets,
// reusing the existing GenericArgCountMismatch diagnostic rather than a
// bespoke error path.
//
// Was the first fixture to surface a real, pre-existing, unrelated sema
// characteristic: a parameter's type annotation used to be resolved
// twice, independently (once in collect_fn_sig during signature
// collection, again in seed_param during body-seeding), so an error on
// a param's own type reported twice at the same span. Tracked as Open
// Decision #6 (docs/MEMORY_MODEL.md §12) and fixed in a later session:
// seed_param now reuses the type collect_fn_sig/collect_method_sig
// already resolved instead of resolving it again from scratch. See
// tests/fixtures/err_param_type_reported_once_isolated.ubl and
// ok_param_type_single_resolution_isolated.ubl for fixtures targeting
// that fix directly.
// Expected: sema FAIL (GenericArgCountMismatch), reported exactly ONCE.

fn bad(x: Unique) void {}

fn main() void {
}
